    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0257" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G/374: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-09T11:00:00-03:00">December 9, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 9—10:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Department’s instructions page 81.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d77-f1"/> Telegraph
                    subsequent changes or contemplated changes if any in Latin American truce <pb
                        facs="0258" n="170" xml:id="pg170"/> membership. Referring to Treaty
                    Information, July, pages 11–13, should Bolivia and Ecuador be considered
                    members?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
